    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A kingdom on the northern shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-victoria">Lake Victoria</a> that rose from a small state to the dominant power of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-lakes">Great Lakes</a> by 1800.</li><li>Its kabakas ruled through appointed chiefs, with a council, a chief minister and a fleet of war canoes on the lake.</li><li>Buganda gave its name to Uganda; abolished in 1967, the monarchy was restored as a cultural institution in 1993.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Because princes belonged to their mothers’ clans, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baganda">Ganda</a> royal family had no clan of its own, and any clan could hope to provide a future kabaka.</p></aside>
    </section>

